 by 10. Finally, if the sum (even after adjustment) exceeds 21, function returns 'BUST'.", "created_at": "2022-07-08T16:36:56Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f60f12ea1ea3c990ad1126eda395f3d8db7bd5c4", "message": "Create charTimesThree\n\nMultiplies every character in a given string by three.", "created_at": "2022-07-08T13:05:00Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ccfb9f0797583bcfa2d899fbd20ab7b7995a54b9", "message": "Create areThreesInYourList\n\nThis program let's you declare size of a list, fill that list with numbers and then it finds out if there are any threes adjacent to each other in that list.", "created_at": "2022-07-08T02:29:22Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5413da334ae376006ce34a383b640a4900503a25", "message": "Create reverseSentence\n\nReverses input sentence.", "created_at": "2022-07-08T01:32:44Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "346eb04fc8219319791b61e989491bfbf18dada2", "message": "Create capitalize\n\nCapitalizes 1st and 4th letter in a given word.", "created_at": "2022-07-08T01:17:02Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "43a9eb500bb328c2dba91eeca50cdb3f671852d1", "message": "Create jadenCase2\n\nSame as previous program under the same name, but this time it's executed with less code.", "created_at": "2022-07-07T23:38:06Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "692cc76852898c8690643ddb0f082b3417833b74", "message": "Create jadenCase\n\nThis will make your input sentence look like it was tweeted by Jaden Smith.\r\n\r\n.title() method would capitalize every character after an upper dash ( ' ) so it won't work here. Simply enough splitting a string into a list, iterating every element in that list with a .capitalize() and joining the list back together into a string is what works best.", "created_at": "2022-07-07T14:14:59Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a62c7d6ed70e9372b3bd306b1440f36b8acc3ecf", "message": "Update disemvowel", "created_at": "2022-07-07T13:08:16Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9d70c6b87f060494492eab299341c909dce2f544", "message": "Create disemvowel\n\nFunction, that disemvowels a provided sentence.", "created_at": "2022-07-06T16:28:52Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0c83034ed8ee81a05882f4d9d3d1de82ac9506d2", "message": "Create GuessingGame\n\nGuess a number between 1 and 100 and see if it matches the one picked by this program.", "created_at": "2022-06-30T00:05:08Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "343c6f46ad5e4743669039d88c66eb991403d747", "message": "Create KidsCollectingStrawberries\n\nThis is something that I was supposed to do with a bunch of FOR loops, but I've failed miserably over and over to realize how to avoid berries being a global variable, so in the end I've given up and decided to just declare a function that calculates the loop inside and only returns a print statement, instead of overwriting the global variable. Now github copilot neatly suggested to globalize my berries inside the function body and for some rookie reason taken his suggestion, which ended up overwriting my berries yet again. Eventually I realized I just need to move berries completely into the function body and that did it. Now it works as intended.", "created_at": "2022-06-27T22:16:59Z", "repo": "Python_scripts", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a4